From: OmacVM
Subject: [PATCH] ui: one pointer between the VM and Omanotch's strip in full screen

What: when the pointer leaves a view of the VM up into Omanotch's strip
(macOS full screen below a notch, absolute pointer, VM has it), QEMU sends
one last tablet position: the top row of the guest's hidden NOTCH output,
behind the camera (ui/omacvm-notch-park.h). The main view and the views of
the other outputs (with an external display holding the main window, the
MacBook's display is one of those). The guest's layout message now also
keeps NOTCH's box. Nothing else changes: the next motion over the VM
brings the guest's pointer back, as before.

Why: since full screen moved to its own Space (3.0.x), the strip is
another app's window above ours. QEMU shows the Mac's arrow at once when
the pointer leaves, but the guest's arrow stayed on the VM's top rows until
notchcast hid it with Hyprland's cursor:invisible, which Hyprland applies
only on a periodic tick (85-540 ms measured on the MacBook Air): two arrows
on the way up, and on the way back no arrow until it was shown again.
With the guest's pointer out of sight in NOTCH, the guest never has to hide
it (notchcast reads omacvm.notchpointer=1, sent by OmacVM.app). Measured
on the Air, 20 crossings each way (frames with a missing / an extra
cursor): slow moves 255/98 -> 14/0, fast moves 37/251 -> 4/63 (single
frames of render latency), tracks/notch-cursor-flicker.md.

Upstream: not applicable (OmacVM's notch strip).
Test: app/runtime/Tests/display/test-notch-park.c (the logic);
src/tests/notch-cursor-flicker/ (recording on a notched Mac, manual).

